{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1122","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1122","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1122\",\"parent_revision\":\"b48a18fb75abe94019a2b4e6f5d89e8e862e153938f5b76b5cf2642d4cd8e24d\",\"root_revision\":\"b48a18fb75abe94019a2b4e6f5d89e8e862e153938f5b76b5cf2642d4cd8e24d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-04-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThree issues in `tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py`:\\n\\n1. **Private symbol imports** (line 26): `_write_cache` and `_write_github_issue_field` imported and called directly, bypassing the public CLI surface.\\n\\n2. **Dual-patch conflict** in `test_skips_already_migrated` (lines 188\u2013190): `patch()` context managers active while also setting `mod.create_task_issue = mock_create` directly \u2014 unclear which patch is in effect.\\n\\n3. **`except SystemExit: pass`** in `test_partial_failure_continues` (lines 307\u2013310): swallows crashes. The test asserts on file content that may not have been written because the CLI crashed. Also uses fragile manual `try/finally` for `mod._BACKLOG_CORE` save/restore.\\n\\nFix:\\n- Replace `_write_cache`/`_write_github_issue_field` direct calls with CLI-level `CliRunner` invocations\\n- Remove direct attribute assignments; rely solely on `patch()` context managers  \\n- Remove `try/except SystemExit: pass`; use `mocker.patch.object` for `_BACKLOG_CORE`; assert `result.exit_code` explicitly\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-29T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix broken patching and private imports in test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-29T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Test quality audit 2026-03-29\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nRun the affected tests to observe current failures and anti-patterns:\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run pytest tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py -v\\n```\\n\\nThe three issues are observable in the test file without running:\\n\\n1. Line 26 imports private symbols `_write_cache` and `_write_github_issue_field` directly.\\n2. Lines 178\u2013191 (`test_skips_already_migrated`) both enters `patch()` context managers **and** sets `mod.create_task_issue = mock_create` and `mod.get_github = mock_gh` directly on the module \u2014 two patches compete.\\n3. Lines 307\u2013310 (`test_partial_failure_continues`) has `try: runner.invoke(..., catch_exceptions=False) / except SystemExit: pass` which silences crashes, plus manual `mod._BACKLOG_CORE = orig_bc` restore instead of a pytest fixture.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Run `uv run pytest tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py::test_partial_failure_continues -v` \u2014 test may pass even when the CLI crashes before writing the file, because the `except SystemExit: pass` block absorbs the failure and the assertion runs on stale content.\\n- Read `tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py` lines 26, 178\u2013200, 289\u2013316 to observe all three anti-patterns in source.\\n- The private imports at line 26 bypass the import guard that limits `_write_cache` and `_write_github_issue_field` to internal use \u2014 any signature change in the script will silently break these tests.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Tests for a migration script are a safety net against regressions. The `except SystemExit: pass` pattern means a crashing CLI produces a false-passing test, which is the most dangerous failure mode. The dual-patch conflict makes the test unreliable on mock execution order. Fixing these makes the test suite trustworthy for future changes to `migrate_tasks_to_github.py`.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: confidence in `migrate_tasks_to_github.py` changes \u2014 a broken CLI passes tests silently.\\n- Bottleneck: any refactor of `_write_cache` or `_write_github_issue_field` signatures breaks two tests with no warning about the real regression.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Tests will catch CLI crashes rather than silently pass.\\n- Mock patching is unambiguous \u2014 the active mock is always the one from the `patch()` context manager.\\n- Private symbol changes in the script no longer silently invalidate test logic.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nEach test invokes the CLI via `CliRunner` and asserts on `result.exit_code`. Mocks are applied exclusively through `patch()` context managers. No direct module attribute assignments. `_BACKLOG_CORE` is patched with `mocker.patch.object` or `patch()`, not set manually with a `try/finally` restore. A CLI crash causes a non-zero `result.exit_code`, which the test asserts on explicitly.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `test_writes_github_issue_field`: invokes the CLI with a task file lacking `github_issue`, patches `create_task_issue` to return a mock issue dict, asserts `github_issue: 481` appears in the written file and `result.exit_code == 0`.\\n- `test_writes_cache_file`: invokes the CLI via `CliRunner`, patches `create_task_issue` and `_BACKLOG_CORE`, asserts the cache JSON file is written with the expected structure.\\n- `test_skips_already_migrated`: uses only `patch()` context managers, no direct `mod.X =` assignments.\\n- `test_partial_failure_continues`: no `try/except SystemExit`; uses `catch_exceptions=True` (default) and asserts `result.exit_code != 0` or uses `mocker.patch.object` for `_BACKLOG_CORE`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run pytest tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py -v` exits 0 with all tests passing.\\n2. Line 26 of `tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py` imports only public symbols (`app`, `parse_task_file`, `infer_task_type`) \u2014 no `_write_cache` or `_write_github_issue_field` imports.\\n3. `test_writes_github_issue_field` uses `CliRunner.invoke()` and asserts `result.exit_code == 0`; no direct call to `_write_github_issue_field`.\\n4. `test_writes_cache_file` uses `CliRunner.invoke()` and asserts the cache JSON file exists and contains the expected structure; no direct call to `_write_cache`.\\n5. `test_skips_already_migrated` contains no `mod.create_task_issue =` or `mod.get_github =` direct assignments.\\n6. `test_partial_failure_continues` contains no `except SystemExit` and no manual `mod._BACKLOG_CORE = orig_bc` restore; `result.exit_code` is asserted explicitly.\\n7. `uv run prek run --files tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py` exits 0 (no linting regressions).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Script under test | `plugins/python3-development/scripts/migrate_tasks_to_github.py` |\\n| Test file | `tests/test_migrate_tasks_to_github.py` |\\n| Agent | `@python3-development:python-pytest-architect` |\\n| Public CLI surface | `app` (Typer), `CliRunner` already used in `test_dry_run_no_writes` (line 136\u2013159) |\\n| Pytest config | `pyproject.toml` \u2014 `testpaths` includes `tests`, scripts dir in `pythonpath` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 self-contained test file fix.\\n- Blocks: None directly; improves safety net for future `migrate_tasks_to_github.py` changes.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all three issues are fully locatable in the test file, the public CLI surface (`CliRunner`, `app`) is already demonstrated in `test_dry_run_no_writes`, and `mocker.patch.object` is available via `pytest-mock`.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 three isolated test functions, no production code changes required. The fix pattern (replace direct call with `CliRunner.invoke`) is already demonstrated by `test_dry_run_no_writes` in the same file.\\n\",\"digest\":\"a9b9bfaa4a6e9e2ec51e7e0fe170362725978e87de5b